info:
  title: URL Shortener
  version: 0.1.0
paths:
  /api/links:
    post:
      operationId: createLink
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema: {$ref: '#/components/schemas/CreateLinkRequest'}
      responses:
        '201':
          description: Created
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: {$ref: '#/components/schemas/CreateLinkResponse'}
        '400': {$ref: '#/components/responses/Error'}
        '409': {$ref: '#/components/responses/Error'}
        '429':
          description: RATE_LIMITED
          headers:
            Retry-After: {schema: {type: integer}}
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: {$ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody'}
  /api/links/{code}/stats:
    get:
      operationId: getStats
      parameters:
        - {name: code, in: path, required: true, schema: {type: string}}
        - {name: X-Management-Token, in: header, required: false, schema: {type: string}}
        - {name: days, in: query, required: false, schema: {type: integer, minimum: 1, maximum: 90, default: 30}}
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Statistics
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: {$ref: '#/components/schemas/LinkStatsResponse'}
        '400': {$ref: '#/components/responses/Error'}
        '401': {$ref: '#/components/responses/Error'}
  /{code}:
    get:
      operationId: redirect
      parameters:
        - {name: code, in: path, required: true, schema: {type: string}}
      responses:
        '302':
          description: Redirect to the long URL
          headers:
            Location: {schema: {type: string, format: uri}}
        '404': {$ref: '#/components/responses/Error'}
        '410': {$ref: '#/components/responses/Error'}
components:
  responses:
    Error:
      description: Error
      content:
        application/json:
          schema: {$ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody'}
  schemas:
    CreateLinkRequest:
      type: object
      required: [url]
      properties:
        url: {type: string, maxLength: 2048}
        alias: {type: string, pattern: '^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{3,32}$'}
        expiresAt: {type: string, format: date-time}
    CreateLinkResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        shortCode: {type: string}
        shortUrl: {type: string}
        managementToken: {type: string}
        expiresAt: {type: string, format: date-time, nullable: true}
    LinkStatsResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        code: {type: string}
        days: {type: integer}
        clicksPerDay:
          type: array
          items:
            type: object
            properties:
              date: {type: string, format: date}
              count: {type: integer, format: int64}
        topReferrers:
          type: array
          maxItems: 10
          items:
            type: object
            properties:
              host: {type: string}
              count: {type: integer, format: int64}
    ErrorBody:
      type: object
      properties:
        code:
          type: string
          enum: [INVALID_REQUEST, INVALID_URL, UNSAFE_URL, INVALID_ALIAS, ALIAS_TAKEN, INVALID_EXPIRY, UNAUTHORIZED, NOT_FOUND, GONE, RATE_LIMITED, INTERNAL_ERROR]
        message: {type: string}
"},{"path":"docs/SECURITY.md","action":"create","content":"# Security notes

## SSRF and DNS rebinding (residual risk)
The destination host is resolved once at creation through `HostResolver`. The link is rejected if any address is loopback, private, link-local, CGNAT, unique-local, multicast or unspecified, including IPv4-mapped IPv6 and numeric IPv4 encodings.
The service never fetches the destination. It only issues a 302, so it is not itself an SSRF vector.
DNS can change after creation (rebinding). A client that follows the redirect later may reach an address that was never checked. This residual risk is accepted and destinations are not re-resolved at redirect time.

## Management tokens
Each token is 32 bytes from SecureRandom, base64url without padding (256 bits). Only the lowercase hex SHA-256 is stored, and comparison uses `MessageDigest.isEqual`. Tokens travel only in `X-Management-Token`, never in URLs.

## Privacy
Clicks keep only the link, the UTC day, the referrer host and a count.
"},{"path":"docs/design.md","action":"create","content":"# URL Shortener: Design

Base package `com.agentic.shortener`. Spring Boot 3.4, JPA with Flyway (PostgreSQL in prod, H2 in tests), Redis behind a port.

## Components
- **Shared (this task, read-only for implementers):** `config.AppConfig` (Clock bean `Clock.systemUTC()`, `@EnableScheduling`), `config.ShortenerProperties` (prefix `shortener`, every value has an in-code default), `common.ErrorCode`, `common.ErrorBody(code,message)`, `common.ApiException(ErrorCode,String)`, `common.RateLimitedException(long retryAfterSeconds)` and `common.GlobalExceptionHandler`.
- **Ports** `ports.api`: `HostResolver`, `LinkCache` with `CachedLink`, `ClickRecorder`, `ClickBatchWriter` with `ClickEvent`.
- **API contracts** `api`: `LinkService`, `RedirectService`, `StatsService`, `UrlValidator`, `CreationRateLimiter` and the DTO records.
- **Domain** `domain`: entities `Link` and `Click`, `LinkRepository`, `ClickRepository`, projections `DayCount` and `ReferrerCount`.

## Data model (exact names for the SCHEMA task: `src/main/resources/db/migration/V1__init.sql`)
Table `links`:
- `id` BIGINT GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY
- `code` VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL, UNIQUE constraint `uk_links_code`
- `long_url` VARCHAR(2048) NOT NULL
- `token_hash` VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL (lowercase hex SHA-256 of the token)
- `created_at` TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE NOT NULL
- `expires_at` TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE NULL (null means never expires)
- index `ix_links_expires_at` on (`expires_at`)

Table `click_daily`:
- `id` BIGINT GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY
- `link_id` BIGINT NOT NULL, FK `fk_click_daily_link` references `links(id)`
- `click_day` DATE NOT NULL (UTC day)
- `referrer_host` VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL (`(direct)` when there is no referrer)
- `click_count` BIGINT NOT NULL
- UNIQUE `uk_click_daily` (`link_id`, `click_day`, `referrer_host`)

There are no IP, user-agent, path, full-referrer or timestamp columns. The SQL must run on both H2 and PostgreSQL.

## HTTP contract (`src/main/resources/openapi/api.yaml`)
- `POST /api/links` returns 201 `CreateLinkResponse`. Errors: 400 (INVALID_URL, UNSAFE_URL, INVALID_ALIAS, INVALID_EXPIRY, INVALID_REQUEST), 409 ALIAS_TAKEN, 429 RATE_LIMITED with `Retry-After`.
- `GET /{code}` returns 302 with `Location`. Errors: 404 NOT_FOUND, 410 GONE. Error bodies never carry a Location header.
- `GET /api/links/{code}/stats?days=` with header `X-Management-Token` returns 200 `LinkStatsResponse`. Errors: 401 UNAUTHORIZED, 400 INVALID_REQUEST when days is outside 1-90.

## Rules
- **URL:** at most 2048 chars, absolute, scheme `http` or `https` (case-insensitive), non-empty host. Otherwise INVALID_URL.
- **Resolution:** `HostResolver.resolve(host)` is called exactly once per creation request (also for IP literals; IPv6 brackets are stripped). It is never called on redirect.
  - `UnknownHostException` or an empty result gives INVALID_URL.
  - If any address is blocked, the result is UNSAFE_URL.
  - Numeric IPv4 hosts in decimal, hex, octal or shortened form (e.g. `2130706433`, `0x7f.1`, `0177.0.0.1`) are also decoded locally and checked.
- **Blocked ranges:**
  - IPv4: 0/8, 10/8, 100.64/10, 127/8, 169.254/16, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, 224/4, 240/4
  - IPv6: `::`, `::1`, fc00::/7, fe80::/10, ff00::/8, plus `::ffff:a.b.c.d` checked as IPv4
- **Alias:** `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{3,32}$`, case-sensitive. Reserved names (`shortener.links.reserved-aliases`, compared case-insensitively) give INVALID_ALIAS. An existing code gives ALIAS_TAKEN, and the original link is unchanged.
- **Generated code:** 7 base62 chars from SecureRandom, retried on collision (at most 5 attempts).
- **Expiry:** optional ISO-8601 instant string. It must parse (else INVALID_EXPIRY), be after `now`, and be no later than `now + max-expiry`. A link is expired when `expiresAt <= now` (410).
- **Token:** 32 random bytes, base64url without padding. Store `HexFormat.of().formatHex(SHA-256(token UTF-8))` and compare with `MessageDigest.isEqual`.
- **Stats access:** a missing or wrong token, or an unknown code, gives 401. The token check runs against a dummy hash when the code is unknown.
- **Stats contents:**
  - `days` defaults to 30, valid range 1-90.
  - Window start is `today(UTC) - (days-1)`, applied to both lists.
  - `clicksPerDay` is ascending by date and lists only days with clicks.
  - `topReferrers` holds at most 10 entries, sorted by count descending.
- **Referrer:** host of the Referer URI, lower-cased. A missing or unparsable referrer, or one without a host, becomes `(direct)`. The click day is `LocalDate.now(clock)` in UTC.
- **Redirect lookup:**
  1. Try `LinkCache.get`. Any exception or timeout is logged at WARN and treated as a miss.
  2. On a miss, run `LinkRepository.findByCode`. If found, call `LinkCache.put`, guarded the same way.
  3. Check expiry against the Clock even for cached entries.
  4. Then call `ClickRecorder.record(code, referer)`.
- **Rate limit:** fixed window per client key using the Clock.
  - The key is `request.getRemoteAddr()`; when `shortener.rate-limit.trusted-proxy=true`, it is the first `X-Forwarded-For` entry instead.
  - It is checked in `POST /api/links` before validation.
  - Retry-After is the number of seconds until the window ends.
  - Redirects are never limited.
- **Clicks:**
  - `ArrayBlockingQueue` of `clicks.queue-capacity`, filled with `offer()` (never blocks).
  - A full queue, an unknown code or a writer exception increments the Micrometer counter `shortener.clicks.dropped` by the number of events lost.
  - A worker drains up to `clicks.batch-size` events every `clicks.flush-interval` or as soon as a batch is full.
- **Retention:** `@Scheduled(cron = "${shortener.retention.cron:0 30 3 * * *}")` calls `ClickRepository.deleteForLinksExpiredBefore(now - retention.after-expiry)` in a transaction. Links themselves are kept.

## Implementation tasks, owned packages and classes
All implementation classes are Spring `@Component`, `@Service` or `@RestController` beans with constructor injection. Implementers must not edit shared files.

**IMPLEMENT-SCHEMA** owns `src/main/resources/db/migration/` and creates `V1__init.sql` exactly as specified above.

**IMPLEMENT-SAFETY** owns `com.agentic.shortener.safety`:
- `InetHostResolver implements HostResolver`: built from `(ShortenerProperties)`, uses `InetAddress.getAllByName` bounded by `resolver.timeout`.
- `BlockedAddresses`: final utility class with `static boolean isBlocked(InetAddress)` and `static Optional<InetAddress> parseNumericIpv4(String host)`.
- `DefaultUrlValidator implements UrlValidator`: built from `(HostResolver)`.

**IMPLEMENT-LINKS** owns `com.agentic.shortener.links`:
- `TokenHasher`: final utility class with `static String sha256Hex(String token)`.
- `FixedWindowCreationRateLimiter implements CreationRateLimiter`: built from `(ShortenerProperties, Clock)`.
- `DefaultLinkService implements LinkService`: built from `(LinkRepository, UrlValidator, ShortenerProperties, Clock)`, `@Transactional`.
- `LinkController`: built from `(LinkService, CreationRateLimiter, ShortenerProperties)`, maps `POST /api/links`.

**IMPLEMENT-REDIRECT** owns `com.agentic.shortener.redirect`:
- `RedisLinkCache implements LinkCache`: built from `(StringRedisTemplate, ShortenerProperties)`. Stores `linkId|expiresEpochMillis-or-empty|longUrl` with `cache.ttl` under `cache.key-prefix + code`.
- `DefaultRedirectService implements RedirectService`: built from `(LinkCache, LinkRepository, ClickRecorder, Clock)`.
- `RedirectController`: built from `(RedirectService)`, maps `GET /{code:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}}` and reads the optional `Referer` header.

**IMPLEMENT-STATS** owns `com.agentic.shortener.stats`:
- `JpaClickBatchWriter implements ClickBatchWriter`: built from `(LinkRepository, ClickRepository)`, `@Transactional`. It increments existing rows and otherwise saves a new `Click`.
- `QueueClickRecorder implements ClickRecorder`: built from `(ClickBatchWriter, MeterRegistry, ShortenerProperties, Clock)`.
  - Public `int flush()` drains and writes one batch and returns the number of events taken.
  - Background flushing uses `@Scheduled(fixedDelayString = "${shortener.clicks.flush-interval:1s}")`.
- `DefaultStatsService implements StatsService`: built from `(LinkRepository, ClickRepository, ShortenerProperties, Clock)`.
- `StatsController`: built from `(StatsService)`, maps `GET /api/links/{code}/stats`.
- `ClickRetentionJob`: built from `(ClickRepository, ShortenerProperties, Clock)`, public `int purge()` returns the rows deleted.

## Testing guidance
- Use `@SpringBootTest` + `@AutoConfigureMockMvc` on H2. No test needs Redis, Docker or network.
- Replace beans with `@MockitoBean` or a `@TestConfiguration` declaring a `@Primary` bean of type `Clock`, `HostResolver`, `LinkCache` or `ClickBatchWriter`.
- Read the dropped-click metric with `meterRegistry.get("shortener.clicks.dropped").counter().count()`.
- To avoid the creation limit, give each request a unique `remoteAddr` via a MockMvc request post-processor, or set `shortener.rate-limit.requests-per-window` in the test properties.
"}],"decisions":[{"title":"Ports package is com.agentic.shortener.ports.api","context":"The task asks for package com.agentic.shortener.ports, but the architect may only write packages ending in .api, .domain, .common or .config.","options":["com.agentic.shortener.ports.api","com.agentic.shortener.domain.ports","Leave ports to implementers"],"choice":"com.agentic.shortener.ports.api","rationale":"It keeps the ports naming, satisfies the path rules and keeps ports separate from JPA domain types."},{"title":"expiresAt accepted as a string and parsed by the service","context":"AC4 requires a malformed timestamp to return 400 with a specific error code.","options":["Instant field parsed by Jackson","String field parsed by LinkService"],"choice":"String parsed in LinkService","rationale":"This yields a deterministic INVALID_EXPIRY instead of a generic Jackson deserialization error."},{"title":"Extra error codes INVALID_REQUEST and INTERNAL_ERROR","context":"Malformed JSON, a bad days parameter and unexpected failures need an error code too.","options":["Reuse listed codes","Add INVALID_REQUEST and INTERNAL_ERROR"],"choice":"Add both","rationale":"Mislabelling these as INVALID_URL would mislead clients."},{"title":"Click aggregates use a portable increment-then-insert","context":"Upsert syntax differs between H2 and PostgreSQL.","options":["Native ON CONFLICT / MERGE","JPQL update, insert when 0 rows updated"],"choice":"JPQL update then insert, with a unique constraint and '(direct)' stored as a value","rationale":"A single node has a single flush worker, so there is no write race. It is portable, and storing '(direct)' instead of NULL avoids NULLs in the unique key."},{"title":"Column names click_day and click_count","context":"DAY and COUNT are keywords in H2 and SQL.","options":["day/count","click_day/click_count"],"choice":"click_day/click_count, while entity fields stay day/count","rationale":"This avoids quoting issues on both H2 and PostgreSQL."},{"title":"Properties carry in-code defaults","context":"src/test/resources/application.yml shadows the main application.yml in tests.","options":["Require properties in YAML","@DefaultValue on every property"],"choice":"@DefaultValue everywhere","rationale":"The context starts in tests without duplicating configuration."},{"title":"Unknown code on the stats endpoint returns 401","context":"AC11 forbids revealing link existence through the stats endpoint.","options":["404 for unknown code","401 with constant-time dummy hash comparison"],"choice":"401 for an unknown code too","rationale":"A wrong or missing token is indistinguishable from a nonexistent link."},{"title":"Resolver is called once for every host, including literals","context":"AC8 and AC9 require blocking literal encodings and exactly one resolver call per creation request.","options":["Parse literals only, skipping the resolver","Always resolve once and also decode numeric IPv4 locally"],"choice":"Always resolve once, plus a local numeric IPv4 decode","rationale":"Behaviour is uniform, and alternative encodings are blocked even if the resolver accepts them."}]}
